From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui, explorer: a click in the notification centre reaches the program that sent it

The notification centre (sg-shell's sg-notify, the history of 0815) could
only open a toast's link: clicking any other notification did nothing, so
a mail or chat notification read later could not take the person to the
message. Windows hands that click to the program that sent it, and now so
do we, by our own means:
 - every history entry keeps who takes a click: the program's
   AppUserModelID, its file and process, the toast's number there, the
   window of that process that receives it (a message-only window of
   windows.ui's toast thread), and the program's COM toast activator --
   CustomActivator under Software\Classes\AppUserModelId\<id>, or the
   System.AppUserModel.ToastActivatorCLSID of its Start menu shortcut with
   that AppUserModelID (0821); a balloon's entry keeps its icon's window,
   id, callback message and version;
 - windows.ui exports SgActivateNotification( entry, arguments ), which the
   centre calls: a link is opened; a program with an activator gets
   INotificationActivationCallback::Activate( AppUserModelID, the launch
   arguments ) -- COM starts it if it is not running (its per-user
   LocalServer32: 0820); a running program that still holds the toast gets
   its Activated event (WM_COPYDATA to its window, the event raised as
   for a click on screen, on the handler's own apartment); a balloon's icon
   gets NIN_BALLOONUSERCLICK; otherwise the program comes to the front, or
   is started if it has gone;
 - INotificationActivationCallback is declared
   (include/notificationactivationcallback.idl) and its proxy is in
   actxprxy, so the call crosses processes;
 - a click on the toast on screen also calls the program's activator, as
   Windows does, and an activated toast leaves the centre; a toast that
   replaces another by tag replaces it in the centre too, and
   ToastNotificationHistory's Remove/Clear remove entries there.

Test: test/toastactivate-gate.sh with test/toastactivate-probe.c (mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_CENTRE_ACTIVATION, SG_MUTANT_NO_TOAST_ACTIVATOR); the toast and
notifycentre gates still pass.
